bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">finely chopped onions</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">egg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">beaten for binding</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6879-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6879\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For baking the patties.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For frying the patties.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6879-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6879-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6879\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6879-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat your oven to 200°C (400°F) or heat a skillet over medium heat. This is the first step to crispy perfection!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6879-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Carefully place the frozen chicken patties on a baking sheet or in the skillet. Make sure they have a little space to breathe!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6879-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Bake for 18–20 minutes, flipping halfway through, or cook in the skillet for 5–6 minutes per side until they are golden brown and fully cooked. Keep an eye on them; you want them just right!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6879-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Remove the patties from the oven or skillet and let them rest for 1–2 minutes before serving. This helps them stay juicy and delicious!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-6879-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>250</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather all your ingredients to whip up some delicious chicken <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patty\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">patties</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Homemade-Chicken-Patties.webp\" alt=\"Fresh ingredients for chicken patties displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-6877\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Homemade-Chicken-Patties.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Homemade-Chicken-Patties-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups</strong> – diced cooked chicken</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cup</strong> – <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breadcrumbs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">breadcrumbs</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup</strong> – grated Parmesan cheese</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup</strong> – finely chopped onions</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp</strong> – garlic powder</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp</strong> – black pepper</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp</strong> – salt</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 egg</strong> – beaten for binding</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-chicken-patties-frozen\"><strong>How to Make chicken patties frozen</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to enjoy some delicious chicken patties! With a prep time of just 5 minutes, cooking time of 18–20 minutes, and a little resting time of 1–2 minutes, you’ll have a tasty meal in no time!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Chicken-Patties-Frozen.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of preparing chicken patties frozen, from preheating the oven to serving the cooked patties.\" class=\"wp-image-6878\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Chicken-Patties-Frozen.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparing-Chicken-Patties-Frozen-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 200°C (400°F) or heat a skillet over medium heat. This is the first step to crispy perfection!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Place the Patties</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Carefully place the frozen chicken patties on a baking sheet or in the skillet. Make sure they have a little space to breathe!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cook</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake for 18–20 minutes, flipping halfway through, or cook in the skillet for 5–6 minutes per side until they are golden brown and fully cooked. Keep an eye on them; you want them just right!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Rest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the patties from the oven or skillet and let them rest for 1–2 minutes before serving. This helps them stay juicy and delicious!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Snacks</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>2 minutes resting</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>27 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>High Protein</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and crispy!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-chicken-patties-frozen\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making chicken patties frozen</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use ground chicken for a leaner option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add breadcrumbs for a crispy texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Season the mixture well for maximum flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chill the patties before freezing to maintain shape.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cook from frozen for a quick and easy meal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-chicken-patties-frozen\"><strong>How to Serve this chicken patties frozen</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with a side of crispy sweet potato fries for a delightful crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh avocado slices and a dollop of Greek yogurt for a creamy twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a zesty coleslaw for a refreshing contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sandwich between whole grain buns with lettuce and tomato for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of tangy barbecue sauce for dipping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a vibrant mixed greens salad drizzled with balsamic vinaigrette.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap in a tortilla with salsa and cheese for a fun twist.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to store and enjoy your chicken patties frozen:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow patties to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or wrap tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date for easy tracking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool cooked patties completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Arrange in a single layer on a baking sheet and freeze for 1-2 hours.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to a freezer-safe bag or container, removing as much air as possible.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and use within 2-3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, reheat in the oven at 375°F (190°C) for 15-20 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use a microwave on medium power for 2-3 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Check that the internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let sit for a minute before serving to enhance texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How do you cook frozen chicken patties?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cooking frozen chicken patties is simple and convenient! You can bake them in the oven at 400°F (200°C) for about 20-25 minutes, flipping halfway through for even cooking. Alternatively, you can pan-fry them on medium heat for about 6-8 minutes on each side until they are golden brown and heated through. For a quicker option, you can also microwave them, but they may not get as crispy. Enjoy your delicious chicken patties with your favorite dipping sauce!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Are chicken patties healthy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chicken patties can be a healthy option, especially if they are made from lean chicken and contain minimal additives. Look for brands that use whole ingredients and avoid those with excessive preservatives or fillers. Pairing them with a side of vegetables or a salad can make for a balanced meal. Always check the nutrition label to make informed choices about your food!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Which frozen chicken tastes like Chick-fil-A?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>If you&#8217;re craving that Chick-fil-A flavor, look for frozen chicken patties that are seasoned with a blend of spices similar to their famous breading. Some brands offer products specifically marketed as &#8216;Chick-fil-A style&#8217; chicken patties. You can also try marinating your patties in a mixture of pickle juice and spices before cooking to replicate that signature taste!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Are Tyson chicken patties real chicken?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, Tyson chicken patties are made from real chicken. They typically use chicken breast meat and other ingredients to create their patties. However, it&#8217;s always a good idea to check the packaging for specific ingredient information to ensure you&#8217;re getting the quality you expect. Tyson is known for its commitment to providing quality poultry products!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So there you have it—delicious chicken patties frozen, ready to bring joy to your table! They’re simple to make, and the satisfaction of biting into a crispy, flavorful patty is unbeatable. Gather your loved ones, whip up a batch, and enjoy the delightful memories that come with every bite. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
